    "Here is a simple implementation of state abstraction for this grid world problem using Python:\n\n```python\nclass StateAbstraction:\n    def __init__(self, grid_world):\n        self.grid = grid_world[\"grid\"]\n        self.rows = len(self.grid)\n        self.cols = len(self.grid[0])\n        \n        # Identify the goal position\n        self.goal_row = self.rows - 1\n        self.goal_col = self.cols - 1\n\n    def group_states(self, state):\n        # Get row and column of current state\n        for i in range(self.rows):\n            for j in range(self.cols):\n                if self.grid[i][j] == state:\n                    return [i // (self.rows // 3), j // (self.cols // 3)]\n\n    def abstract_states(self, num_abstract_states):\n        # Group states into abstract states\n        abstract_state_grouping = []\n        for _ in range(num_abstract_states):\n            row_group = []\n            for _ in range(num_abstract_states):\n                col_group = []\n                for state in range(len(self.grid) * len(self.grid[0])):\n                    if self.group_states(state) == [len(abstract_state_grouping), len(row_group)]:\n                        col_group.append(state)\n                row_group.append(col_group)\n            abstract_state_grouping.append(row_group)\n\n        return abstract_state_grouping\n\n\n# Test the code\ngrid_world = {\"goal\":52,\"grid\":[[0,2,5,9,13,15,17,19,23],[1,4,8,12,\"X\",\"X\",\"X\",22,25],[3,7,\"X\",\"X\",59,56,\"X\",\"X\",27],[6,11,\"X\",\"X\",57,53,\"X\",33,29],[10,\"X\",58,54,\"X\",49,41,37,32],[14,\"X\",55,50,42,\"X\",48,\"X\",36],[16,\"X\",\"X\",\"X\",38,43,\"X\",47,40],[18,21,\"X\",30,34,\"X\",44,51,46],[20,24,26,28,31,35,39,45,52]],\"start\":0}\nstate_abstraction = StateAbstraction(grid_world)\nabstract_states = state_abstraction.abstract_states(3)\n\nprint(abstract_states)\n\n```\n\nThe code uses a simple form of abstraction by dividing the grid world into 9 abstract states (dividing both dimensions in three). Each abstract state contains all original states that fall within its boundaries.",
